            "commit": "7c3c9f8814bbf0d4fb9016f718d4a70332343058",
            "subject": "LU-20076 tests: evict failed clients at once in insanity"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-01 19:47:33.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 08:36:31.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-16507 lmv: refresh the statfs of every NOCREATE MDT",
        "message": "LU-16507 lmv: refresh the statfs of every NOCREATE MDT\n\nThe QoS and round-robin mkdir allocators skip an MDT marked NOCREATE,\nand lmv_locate_tgt_by_space() only refreshed the statfs of an MDT\npicked by round-robin, and of the parent or requested MDT if it was\nNOCREATE.  Once no_create was cleared on another MDT, the client would\nkeep avoiding that MDT for new directories until something else, like\n\"lfs df\", refreshed its statfs.  sanity test_413a could fail with all\ndirectories on MDT0000 when it ran right after test_413Aa, which\nmarks every MDT NOCREATE.\n\nCheck every active MDT marked NOCREATE in lmv_locate_tgt_by_space(),\nthose other than the parent or requested MDT only every\n4 * qos_maxage, since NOCREATE is usually set for a long time.\nRecord when any async statfs request is sent to an MDT, and send no\nother request to that MDT for 2 seconds, rather than one more for each\nmkdir until the reply arrives.  The statfs age still says when the\nlast reply arrived.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=112b,ONLY_REPEAT=10\nFixes: 1dbcd0bab881 (\"LU-12998 mds: add no_create parameter to stop creates\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I603b2c6c2cdcc400b7dd29a533267a37cc3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
